1
00:10:49,411 --> 00:10:55,411
Ice is a thriller, action, science fiction film directed by Nick Copus.

2
00:21:38,823 --> 00:21:44,823
It is 2020.

3
00:32:28,235 --> 00:32:34,235
Findings by environmental scientist Professor Thom Archer suggest that Halo, the corporate
energy company drilling on the Greenland Glacier are causing it to melt.

4
00:43:17,647 --> 00:43:23,647
Archer's warnings are ignored, so he heads to the
Arctic to find indisputable evidence.

5
00:54:07,058 --> 00:54:13,058
Upon arrival, he realizes humankind is under immediate
threat, and races home to save his family.

6
01:04:56,470 --> 01:05:02,470
The glacier collapses, with devastating consequences.

7
01:15:45,882 --> 01:15:51,882
Astonishing weather patterns emerge and plunge the
world's temperatures into steep decline.

8
01:26:35,294 --> 01:26:41,294
Thom Archer, played by Richard Roxburgh.

9
01:37:24,705 --> 01:37:30,705
Sarah, played by Frances O'Connor.

10
01:48:14,117 --> 01:48:20,117
Jacqueline, played by Claire Forlani.

11
01:59:03,529 --> 01:59:09,529
Stephen, played by Ben Cross.

12
02:09:52,941 --> 02:09:58,941
Peterson, played by Stephen Moyer.

13
02:20:42,352 --> 02:20:48,352
Milly, played by Brooke Williams.

14
02:31:31,764 --> 02:31:37,764
Thin Ice (originally released as The Convincer) is a 2011 American black comedy film
directed by Jill Sprecher and starring Greg Kinnear, Alan Arkin and Billy Crudup.

15
02:42:21,176 --> 02:42:27,176
The film explores themes of climate change, ice age,
polar bear, helicopter pilot, oil rig .

16
02:53:10,588 --> 02:53:16,588
The tone is thought_provoking and intense.
